load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# An exterior algebra: the algebra of the wedge product, where a vector times itself is zero, so products of distinct
# vectors are antisymmetric and measure oriented volume. It is the Clifford algebra of the zero quadratic form, the pure
# antisymmetric corner with no metric. Its graded pieces are the spaces of areas, volumes, and higher oriented extents,
# and the determinant lives in its top degree. The form carries the underlying vector space; the relation that a vector
# wedged with itself is zero is the defining law.
form exterior-algebra
  link space, like vector-space
